---
import "../styles/global.css";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of Service - Striff" description="Striff Terms of Service" canonical="https://striff.io/terms">
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="mb-8 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">Terms of Service</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
      <p class="text-slate-600">Last updated: October 29, 2026</p>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">1. Agreement to Terms</h2>
        <p>By accessing or using the Striff website, the Striff GitHub App, the Striff browser extension or the Striff API (together, the "Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree to these terms, please do not use the Service.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">2. Description of Service</h2>
        <p>Striff produces structural diffs and architectural review of code changes. The Service includes the Striff website, which explains Striff diagrams and their interpretation, and the Striff GitHub App, browser extension and API, which analyse the code changes you submit. Some parts of the Service are free; paid plans are subject to the pricing shown at the time of purchase.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">3. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">3.1 Ownership</p>
        <p>All content on this website, including text, graphics, logos, images, and software, is the property of HADI Technology or its content suppliers and is protected by intellectual property laws.</p>

        <p class="mt-4">3.2 Striff Trademark</p>
        <p>"Striff" is a trademark of HADI Technology. You may not use the Striff name or logo without prior written permission.</p>

        <p class="mt-4">3.3 License</p>
        <p>You may view, download, and print pages from the website for personal, non-commercial purposes, provided you do not remove any copyright or proprietary notices.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">4. User Conduct</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
          <li>Use the Service for any illegal purpose</li>
          <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to our servers or systems</li>
          <li>Interfere with or disrupt the Service or servers connected to the Service</li>
          <li>Use automated tools to scrape or harvest data from the website</li>
          <li>Impersonate any person or entity or misrepresent your affiliation</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">5. Restricted Users and Uses</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">5.1 Military and Weapons Organisations</p>
        <p>You may not use the Service if you are, or are acting on behalf of:</p>
        <ul class="ml-6 list-disc">
          <li>a military, armed force, defence ministry or department, or military or intelligence agency of any country; or</li>
          <li>an organisation whose business includes developing, supplying or operating weapons, weapons systems, or military targeting, intelligence or surveillance systems, where your use is in connection with that part of its business.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="mt-4">5.2 Prohibited Uses</p>
        <p>You may not use the Service to build, operate, maintain or support any system used to commit or facilitate genocide, war crimes, crimes against humanity or serious violations of international humanitarian law, including systems for selecting military targets or for the mass surveillance of a civilian population.</p>

        <p class="mt-4">5.3 Sanctioned Parties</p>
        <p>You may not use the Service if you are named on a sanctions list maintained by the Government of Canada, or if providing the Service to you is prohibited by the laws that apply to us.</p>

        <p class="mt-4">5.4 Regional Availability</p>
        <p>We may limit or withdraw the Service in any country or region. Where the Service is not available in your location, you may not use it, including by concealing your location.</p>

        <p class="mt-4">5.5 Organisations</p>
        <p>If you install, subscribe to or use the Service on behalf of an organisation, you confirm that the organisation is not restricted under this section and will not use the Service in a way it prohibits.</p>

        <p class="mt-4">5.6 Enforcement</p>
        <p>We may refuse, suspend or terminate access to the Service, without prior notice, where we reasonably believe this section applies. We decide in good faith on the information available to us. If we terminate a paid subscription under this section, we will refund any fees paid for the period after termination.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">6. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">6.1 "As Is" Basis</p>
        <p>The Service is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis without warranties of any kind, either express or implied.</p>

        <p class="mt-4">6.2 No Warranties</p>
        <p>We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, timely, secure, or error-free. We do not warrant the accuracy or completeness of the information on the website.</p>

        <p class="mt-4">6.3 Technical Issues</p>
        <p>The website may contain technical inaccuracies or typographical errors. We reserve the right to make changes and corrections at any time without notice.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, HADI Technology shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages resulting from your use or inability to use the Service.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">8. Third-Party Links</h2>
        <p>The Service may contain links to third-party websites such as GitHub. We are not responsible for the content, privacy policies, or practices of any third-party websites. We encourage you to review the privacy policies of any third-party sites you visit.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">9. Analytics</h2>
        <p>We use analytics to understand how visitors use our website. By using the Service, you consent to our collection of analytics data as described in our Privacy Policy.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">10. Termination</h2>
        <p>We reserve the right to terminate or suspend your access to the Service immediately, without prior notice, for any breach of these Terms of Service, including Section 5.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">11. Governing Law</h2>
        <p>These Terms of Service shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada applicable in it. Any disputes arising under these terms shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of the Province of Ontario.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">12. Changes to Terms</h2>
        <p>We reserve the right to modify these Terms of Service at any time. We will notify users of material changes by posting the updated terms on this page and updating the "Last updated" date. Your continued use of the Service after such changes constitutes acceptance of the new terms.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">13. Contact Information</h2>
        <p>For questions about these Terms of Service, please email us at <a href="mailto:hi@haditechnology.com" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700">hi@haditechnology.com</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
